{The most commonly known color gamut might be “NTSC” (established in 1953 by the US FCC), however, it is not a standard color gamut.}

{Sentence 1: The color gamut of a device is defined as the range of colors it can produce or record.}
{Sentence 2: Color gamut is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.}
{Sentence 3: Commonly seen color gamut standards include NTSC, sRGB, AdobeRGB, DCI-P3, EBU, and AppleRGB.}
{Sentence 4: The selection of color gamut depends on one's workflow and requirements, such as photography or video editing.}
{Sentence 5: To maintain color consistency for posting photos online, it is suggested to edit photos in AdobeRGB and convert to sRGB before posting.}

